Future:
Project roadmap to scale up Loblaw customer retention analytics project 
using PySpark, Google Cloud, and machine learning components
Phase 1 – Data Engineering & Scalability---------------------------------------------------
Goal: Transition your notebook-based analysis to a distributed pipeline.

Move raw CSV data to Google Cloud Storage (GCS).

Set up a PySpark pipeline on Dataproc to handle feature engineering:

Purchase frequency, RFM scores, product seasonality.

Window functions for trend detection (7-day/30-day cycles).

Write cleaned data to BigQuery for easy access and analytics.

Phase 2 – Machine Learning Modeling---------------------------------------------------
Goal: Build churn prediction models and validate performance.

Use BigQuery ML or export features to Vertex AI for modeling.

Apply algorithms like Logistic Regression, XGBoost, or LightGBM for churn classification.

Split users by behavior clusters using KMeans or DBSCAN.

Evaluate performance via ROC-AUC, F1, and Precision@k.

Visualize confusion matrix and user segments via Looker Studio.

Phase 3 – Automation & Serving---------------------------------------------------
Goal: Automate the pipeline and simulate real-time decision workflows.

Orchestrate ETL + ML pipeline using Cloud Composer (Airflow).

Save models to GCS and deploy using Vertex AI prediction endpoints.

Create dashboards showing top churn signals and cohort movements.

Simulate “next-best action” strategies for marketing or loyalty interventions.

Phase 4 – Documentation & Delivery---------------------------------------------------
Goal: Wrap project with clear storytelling and reproducibility.

Deliver well-documented GitHub repo with modular scripts and notebooks.

Include a sample README case narrative: “How we saved X% churned users.”
